    "narrative": "The run found a mixed picture. Delivery performance in the north region did worsen, but that decline was not strong enough to stand on its own as a clean service-quality degradation story. Rising order volume did explain the worsening delivery times, and that was the stronger finding.\n\nThe decline in on-time delivery was weakened: there was some evidence for it, but there was also evidence against it. By contrast, the volume explanation was supported with no refuting evidence, so the data pointed more clearly to demand pressure than to a pure drop in service quality.\n\nThe run tested this with two time-series trend analyses and a change-point detection step, then stopped because it had sufficient evidence. Two questions remained open: whether the deterioration was sustained or just a short-lived spike, and whether staffing changes also helped explain the shift.",
    "statement": "Supported: Rising order volume in the north region explains the worsening delivery times over the period under study. | Not supported: On-time delivery performance in the north region has declined over the period under study.",
